HST Office: no-break spaces show no gray box unless formatting marks are shown (Writer).

Writer painted the field shading (View > Field Shadings) on every no-break space (U+00A0) and non-breaking
hyphen (U+2011) whenever the "Non-breaking spaces" display option was on, which it is by default, even with
formatting marks hidden; their tilde/degree marker was drawn only with formatting marks. Documents from Word
with runs of no-break spaces (spacing after "(2) giao nhau", after "Câu 1.") showed gray boxes that Word and
WPS never show: Word shows a no-break space only with its formatting marks, as a degree sign. The shading is now
drawn only while formatting marks are shown, together with the marker; real fields keep their shading.
The narrow no-break space (U+202F) was never shaded and is unchanged.

